# web-structure-data

> **Purpose:** Keep the web app's structure and data flow predictable.
>
> **Applies to:** `apps/web/**`

## Structure
- Use function components only. One component per file.
- Pages live in `src/pages/`. Components live in `src/components/`.
- Routes: `/`, `/app`, `/run/:id`, `/g/:slug`, `/how-we-verify`, and `*` for not found.
- shadcn/ui primitives stay in `src/components/ui/`. Wrap them; do not rewrite them.
- No global state library. Use React state and the URL.

## Data
- Call the API only through the services in `src/services/`, which use the one Axios instance in `src/lib/api-client.ts`.
- Parse every API response with Zod schemas from `@stamp/schema`.
- Read run progress only through the `useRunStream` hook.
- Components and hooks never call Axios, `fetch` or `EventSource` directly. Only services do.

## States
- Every data view handles loading, empty, error and partial states.
- A partial guide shows which sections are Uncertain and offers Retry.
